Description: Linux system optimizer, monitor, disk utility and speed test
 MySysPilot is a local dashboard (served on 127.0.0.1 only) that combines:
  - live CPU, memory, disk I/O, network and sensor monitoring
  - process, systemd service and startup application management
  - system cleaner (APT cache, logs, journal, caches, trash, old snaps)
  - APT/Snap/Flatpak uninstaller and APT repository manager
  - GNOME Disks-style disk utility on UDisks2 (mount, check/repair,
    partition, format, LUKS, SMART, benchmark)
  - disk/partition backup and restore (compressed images, file archives,
    SHA-256 verification, partition-table backup)
  - Docker Engine install and administration (containers, images,
    volumes, networks, Compose) with examples and templates
  - data recovery in the style of TestDisk/PhotoRec: lost partition search
    and table rewrite, NTFS/FAT/exFAT/ext boot and superblock repair,
    NTFS/FAT undelete and file carving, with an undo log
  - duplicate finder and file/text search
  - internet speed test (Cloudflare and LibreSpeed servers)
 Privileged actions are authorized per action through polkit.
